title: Architecture Overview
category: architecture
order: 1
---

## Data lifecycle

Content is authored as Markdoc files, either directly (Obsidian, any text
editor) or through the Keystatic admin UI, then committed to Git. A push to
`main` triggers a GitHub Actions build that runs Astro's static site
generation and publishes the result to GitHub Pages.

## Rendering

Each content collection (`blog`, `docs`, `cheatsheets`) is queried at build
time via `getCollection()`, and every entry is rendered through a single
dynamic route: `[collection]/[slug].astro`. The page shell is static HTML;
the sidebar and markdown body render inside a hydrated React island.
